# Example Wreak spec: a tiny todo CLI.
# Lines starting with # at column 0 are notes for humans; agents ignore them.
# Each block is written in whatever form the thought came in.

# The big picture. I know what I want, not every detail.
text:
	Build a command-line todo manager called `todo`.
	Items are stored as JSON in ~/.todo.json.
	It MUST use only the Python standard library.
	Commands: add, list, done, remove. Output should be compact and readable.

# I know how dispatch should flow, but I don't care about the argparse details.
pseudo-code: --language python --file todo/cli.py
	function main(argv):
		cmd, args <- parse argv with subcommands add/list/done/remove
		items <- load()
		match cmd:
			add(title): append {id: next_id(items), title, done: false}
			list: for each item print "[x]" if done else "[ ]", id, title
			done(id): set item.done = true, error if id not found
			remove(id): delete item, error if id not found
		save(items) unless cmd is list

# I can already see the storage code, so I'm writing it out.
code: --language python --file todo/storage.py
	import json
	import pathlib

	PATH = pathlib.Path.home() / ".todo.json"


	def load():
	    if not PATH.exists():
	        return []
	    return json.loads(PATH.read_text())


	def save(items):
	    PATH.write_text(json.dumps(items, indent=2))

# Packaging and tests: I don't care how they're done, just do them.
text:
	Add a pyproject.toml so `pip install .` exposes the `todo` command.
	Include a few unit tests for the cli module.
